  "interpretation": "<p data-start=\"123\" data-end=\"323\"><strong data-start=\"123\" data-end=\"149\">Immunoglobulin A (IgA)</strong> is an antibody primarily found in mucosal areas such as the respiratory and gastrointestinal tracts. Measuring serum <strong data-start=\"267\" data-end=\"281\">IgA levels</strong> by <strong data-start=\"285\" data-end=\"307\">immunoturbidimetry</strong> helps evaluate:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"325\" data-end=\"449\">\n<li data-start=\"325\" data-end=\"346\">\n<p data-start=\"327\" data-end=\"346\"><strong data-start=\"327\" data-end=\"346\">Immune function</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"347\" data-end=\"371\">\n<p data-start=\"349\" data-end=\"371\"><strong data-start=\"349\" data-end=\"371\">Chronic infections</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"372\" data-end=\"397\">\n<p data-start=\"374\" data-end=\"397\"><strong data-start=\"374\" data-end=\"397\">Autoimmune diseases</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"398\" data-end=\"449\">\n<p data-start=\"400\" data-end=\"449\"><strong data-start=\"400\" data-end=\"418\">IgA deficiency</strong> or <strong data-start=\"422\" data-end=\"449\">monoclonal gammopathies</strong></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start=\"451\" data-end=\"561\">It is often ordered as part of an <strong data-start=\"485\" data-end=\"525\">immunoglobulin panel (IgG, IgA, IgM)</strong> to assess overall humoral immunity.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>IgA Level</th>\n<th>Possible Clinical Indications</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Elevated</td>\n<td>Chronic liver disease (e.g., cirrhosis), chronic respiratory or gastrointestinal infections, autoimmune disorders (e.g., rheumatoid arthritis, SLE, celiac disease), monoclonal gammopathy or IgA multiple myeloma</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Decreased</td>\n<td>Selective IgA deficiency (most common primary immunodeficiency), protein-losing enteropathy, nephrotic syndrome, some congenital or acquired immunodeficiencies (e.g., common variable immunodeficiency)</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p data-start=\"451\" data-end=\"561\">&nbsp;</p>",
